* CABSRT07 - SORT AND SUMMARISE THE BILLING SUMMARY FILE
* MVT SORT/MERGE CONTROL CARD.  SORTS TELCABS.CABS.SUMMARY BY
* OCN, BAN AND JURISDICTION AHEAD OF CABRAT09, WHICH READS THE
* FILE IN THAT ORDER AND ACCUMULATES ONE INVOICE AT A TIME.
*
* TWO RULES HAVE LEFT THIS CARD.  THE FIRST COLLAPSED MULTIPLE
* RATED ELEMENTS FOR THE SAME BAN AND JURISDICTION INTO ONE
* SUMMARY LINE, ADDING THE PACKED AMOUNT AT COLUMN 160 FOR SEVEN
* BYTES.  THE SECOND WAS THE RT-ROUND-RULE ROUNDING THAT
* CABSE35B APPLIED TO THAT SUMMED AMOUNT.  A CONTROL CARD CAN
* NAME ONE E35 ONLY, SO BOTH ARE NOW CARRIED BY CABSXSUM, WHICH
* SUMS THE GROUP FIRST, ROUNDS THE GROUP TOTAL SECOND, AND
* RELEASES THE ACCUMULATED FRACTIONAL CENT RESIDUE AS ONE
* ADJUSTMENT RECORD AT END OF MERGE.  CABSE35B IS NOT NAMED ON
* THIS CARD.  NO CABRAT PROGRAM APPLIES ROUNDING TO THE SUMMARY
* LEVEL AMOUNT - CABRAT09 ACCUMULATES WHAT THE EXIT HANDS BACK,
* SO A READER OF CABRAT09 ALONE WILL CONCLUDE THE SUMMARY IS
* UNROUNDED.  IT IS NOT.
*
* EQUAL KEY HANDLING IS NOT CODED.  DUPLICATE KEYS ARE EXPECTED
* ON THIS SORT, AND CABSXSUM NOW DECIDES WHICH IMAGE SURVIVES A
* GROUP - IT KEEPS THE FIRST RECORD OF THE GROUP AND TAKES THE
* ROUND RULE BYTE FROM THAT SAME RECORD.
*
* NEITHER THE SUMMARISATION NOR THE ROUNDING IS READABLE FROM
* THIS CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(5,4,CH,A,9,13,CH,A,40,1,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(200)
 MODS E35=(CABSXSUM,8192,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
